The '''1853 Gran Sur earthquake''' ({{Langx|mxi|١٨٥٣ غران سور الزلزلة 1853|1853 Grân Sûh azzalzala}}), also known as the '''Great Ivorran earthquake''', struck the [[Maroon Confederacy]], the [[Strait of Ivorra|Ivorran islands]], and northern [[Cerdanya|Tinguiririca]] in the afternoon of 8 November 1853 at around 15:22 local time. In combination with subsequent fires and tsunamis, the earthquake almost completely destroyed [[Axarquía]] and devastated communities around the Strait of Ivorra. 

Seismologists estimate the Gran Sur earthquake had a magnitude of 7.7 or greater on the [[W:Moment magnitude scale|moment magnitude scale]], with its epicenter in the [[Strait of Ivorra]] about 20 km (110 nmi; 120 mi) west-southwest of [[Arrayán Bay]].

Chronologically, it was the third known large scale earthquake to hit the region (following those of 1636 and 1531). Estimates place the death toll in Axarquía alone to be around 18,000, making it one of the deadliest earthquakes in Baliscan history. The earthquake intensified political dysfunction within the Confederacy and led to the end of it's policy of isolationism, ultimately bringing it closer to the government of [[Anyos Federales|Federal Balisca]].

